body.text:
svapnavāsavadattam
  {nāndyante tataḥ praviśati sūtradhāraḥ (BhSv_0:1)}
*{sūtradhāraḥ}* -

{niṣkrāntaḥ (BhSv_1.2:1)}
sthāpanā |
  {praviśya}
*{bhaṭau}* - ussaraha ussaraha ayyā ussaraha (BhSv_1.2:2)
[utsaratotsaratāryāḥ utsarata | ]

body.translated_text:
{He exits.}
Interlude.
  {Entering:}
*{Two soldiers}* — 'Make way! Make way, noble ones! Make way!'
[Make way! Make way, noble ones! Make way!]

body.text:
{tataḥ praviśati kāñcukīyaḥ (BhSv_1.4:2)}
*{kāñcukīyaḥ}* - sambhaṣaka na khalu na khalūtsāraṇā kāryā (BhSv_1.4:3)
paśya

body.translated_text:
{Then <s>Padmāvatī</s> enters with her retinue, and a maidservant.}
*{Maidservant}* — Come, come, my lady princess! Enter this hermitage ground.
[Come, come, my lady princess! Enter this hermitage ground.]

body.text:
{tataḥ praviśaty upaviṣṭā tāpasī (BhSv_1.7:5)}
*{tāpasī}* - sāadaṃ rāadāriāe (BhSv_1.7:6)
[svāgataṃ rājadārikāyāḥ | ]

body.translated_text:
{Then a seated female ascetic enters.}
*{Female ascetic}* — Welcome to the princess!
[Welcome to the princess!]

body.text:
{tataḥ praviśati brahmacārī (BhSv_1.11:1)}
*{brahmacārī}* -
  {ūrdhvam avalokya (BhSv_1.11:2)}
sthito madhyāhnaḥ (BhSv_1.11:3)
dṛḍham asmi pariśrāntaḥ (BhSv_1.11:4)
atha kasmin pradeśe viśramayiṣye (BhSv_1.11:5)
  {parikramya (BhSv_1.11:6)}
bhavatu dṛṣṭam (BhSv_1.11:7)
abhitas tapovanena bhavitavyam (BhSv_1.11:8)
tathā hi

{niṣkrāntā (BhSv_2:7)}
praveśakaḥ |
  {tataḥ praviśati kandukena krīḍantī padmāvatī saparivārā vāsavadattayā saha (BhSv_2:8)}
*{vāsavadattā}* - haḷā eso de kanduo (BhSv_2:9)
[halā eṣa te kandukaḥ | ]

body.translated_text:
{She exits.}
Interlude.
  {Then <s>Padmāvatī</s> enters with her retinue and <s>Vāsavadattā</s>, playing with a ball.}
*{<s>Vāsavadattā</s>}* — Dear friend, here is your ball.
[Dear friend, here is your ball.]

{Then the nurse enters.}
*{Nurse}* — Victory to the princess! Princess, you have been given [in marriage]!
[Victory to the princess! Princess, you have been given!]

{Another maidservant enters.}
*{Maidservant}* — Let the noble lady hasten! Today, it seems, the star is auspicious. Today itself the auspicious betrothal ceremony is to be performed — so says our queen.
[Let the noble lady hasten! Today the star is auspicious. Today itself the auspicious betrothal ceremony is to be performed — so says our queen.]

body.text:
{tathā kurvanti (BhSv_4.2:7)}
*{vidūṣakaḥ}* - tattahodī padumāvadī iha āacchia ṇiggadā bhave (BhSv_4.2:8)
[tatrabhavatī padmāvatīhāgatya nirgatā bhavet | ]

{ceṭī tathā karoti (BhSv_4.2:25)}
*{vidūṣakaḥ}* - avihā avihā ciṭṭhadu ciṭṭhadu dāva bhavaṃ (BhSv_4.2:26)
[aviha aviha tiṣṭhatu tiṣṭhatu tāvad bhavān | ]

{ubhāv upaviśataḥ (BhSv_4.3:3)}
*{rājā}* -
  {avalokya}

body.translated_text:
{He exits.}
*{<s>Padmāvatī</s>}* — Noble sister, the noble lord's face is covered by a veil of tears. Let us withdraw.
[Noble sister, the noble lord's face is covered by a veil of tears. Let us withdraw.]

body.text:
*{vāsavadattā}* - haḷā pavisa (BhSv_4.7:13)
  {ity uktvā niṣkrāntā (BhSv_4.7:14)}
[haḷā praviśa | ]

*{rājā}* - bāḍham (BhSv_4.9:4)
prathamaḥ kalpaḥ (BhSv_4.9:5)
  {utthāya}

{niṣkrāntā (BhSv_5.0:19)}
*{padminikā}* - kahiṃ dāṇiṃ ayyavasantaaṃ pekkhāmi (BhSv_5.0:20)
[kutredānīm āryavasantakaṃ paśyāmi | ]

{tataḥ praviśati vidūṣakaḥ (BhSv_5.0:21)}
*{vidūṣakaḥ}* - ajja khu devīvioavihurahiaassa tattahodo vaccharāassa padumāvadīpāṇiggahaṇasamīriassa accantasuhāvahe maṅgaḷosave madaṇaggidāho ahiadaraṃ vaḍḍhai (BhSv_5.0:22)
  {padminikāṃ vilokya (BhSv_5.0:23)}
ayi padumiṇiā (BhSv_5.0:24)
padumiṇie kiṃ iha vattadi (BhSv_5.0:25)
[adya khalu devīviyogavidhurahṛdayasya tatrabhavato vatsarājasya padmāvatīpāṇigrahaṇasamīritasyātyantasukhāvahe maṅgalotsave madanāgnidāho 'dhikataraṃ vardhate | ayi padminikā | padminike kim iha vartate | ]

{niṣkrāntau (BhSv_5.0:34)} praveśakaḥ
  {tataḥ praviśati rājā (BhSv_5.0:35)}
*{rājā}* -

{praviśya (BhSv_5.1:1)}
*{vidūṣakaḥ}* - tuvaradu tuvaradu dāva bhavaṃ (BhSv_5.1:2)
[tvaratāṃ tvaratāṃ tāvad bhavān | ]

*{rājā}* -
  {praviśyāvalokya sasmitam (BhSv_5.2:13)}
aho sarpavyaktir vaidheyasya (BhSv_5.2:14)

body.translated_text:
*{King}* —
  {Entering and looking, with a smile}
Ah, the serpent-perception of this simpleton!

*{Jester}* —
  {Looking closely}
Sir speaks well. It is indeed not a cobra.
  {Entering and looking about}
The venerable <s>Padmāvatī</s> seems to have come here and gone out again.
[Sir speaks well. It is indeed not a cobra. The venerable <s>Padmāvatī</s> seems to have come here and gone out again.]

body.text:
{niṣkrāntaḥ (BhSv_5.6:16)}
  {tataḥ praviśati vāsavadattā āvantikāveṣeṇa ceṭī ca (BhSv_5.6:17)}
*{ceṭī}* - edu edu ayyā (BhSv_5.6:18)
diḍhaṃ khu bhaṭṭidāriā sīsavedaṇāe dukkhāvidā (BhSv_5.6:19)
[etv etv āryā | dṛḍhaṃ khalu bhartṛdārikā śīrṣavedanayā duḥkhitā | ]

body.translated_text:
{He exits.}
  {Then enter <s>Vāsavadattā</s> in the dress of an <s>Avantī</s> woman, and a maid.}
*{Maid}* — Come, come, noble lady! The princess is indeed greatly afflicted with a headache.
[Come, come, noble lady! The princess is indeed greatly afflicted with a headache.]

body.text:
{ubhe parikrāmataḥ (BhSv_5.6:23)}
*{ceṭī}* - idaṃ samuddagihakaṃ (BhSv_5.6:24)
pavisadu ayyā (BhSv_5.6:25)
jāva ahaṃ vi sīsāṇuḷevaṇaṃ tuvāremi (BhSv_5.6:26)
  {niṣkrāntā (BhSv_5.6:27)}
[idaṃ samudragṛhakam | praviśatv āryā | yāvad aham api śīrṣānulepanaṃ tvarayāmi | ]

body.translated_text:
{Both walk about.}
*{Maid}* — Here is the Ocean Pavilion.
Let the noble lady enter. Meanwhile, I shall hurry to prepare the head-ointment.
  {She exits.}
[Here is the Ocean Pavilion. Let the noble lady enter. Meanwhile, I shall hurry to prepare the head-ointment.]

body.text:
{praviśya (BhSv_5.7:1)}
*{vidūṣakaḥ}* - ai paḍibuddho attabhavaṃ (BhSv_5.7:2)
[ayi pratibuddho 'trabhavān | ]

{niṣkrāntā}
  {tataḥ praviśati kāñcukīyaḥ dhātrī pratīhārī ca (BhSv_6.4:5)}
*{kāñcukīyaḥ}* - bhoḥ

*{rājā}* -
  {sabahumānam (BhSv_6.5:5)}
ārya

body.translated_text:
*{King}* —
  {With great respect:}
Noble sir —

body.text:
*{dhātrī}* - pekkhadu pekkhadu bhaṭṭidāriā (BhSv_6.12:2)
  {citraphalakāṃ darśayati (BhSv_6.12:3)}
[paśyatu paśyatu bhartṛdārikā | ]

body.translated_text:
*{Nurse}* — Let the princess see, let her see!
  {She shows the picture-board.}
[Let the princess see, let her see!]

{Entering:}
*{Door-keeper}* — Victory to the master! A <s>Brāhmaṇa</s> from <s>Ujjayinī</s> has entrusted his 'sister' to the queen's care as a deposit, and he has come to the door to reclaim her.
[Victory to the master! A <s>Brāhmaṇa</s> from <s>Ujjayinī</s> entrusted his 'sister' to the queen as a deposit, and has come to the door to reclaim her.]

body.text:
{tataḥ praviśati yaugandharāyaṇaḥ pratīhārī ca (BhSv_6.14:12)}
*{yaugandharāyaṇaḥ}* - bhoḥ
  {ātmagatam (BhSv_6.14:13)}

*{yaugandharāyaṇaḥ}* - svāmin devyapanayena kṛtāparādhaḥ khalv aham (BhSv_6.17:1)
tat kṣantum arhati svāmī (BhSv_6.17:2)
  {iti pādayoḥ patati (BhSv_6.17:3)}
*{rājā}* -
  {utthāpya (BhSv_6.17:4)}
yaugandharāyaṇo bhavān nanu (BhSv_6.17:5)
